# Hearthwild

- Read `docs/hearthwild/README.md`, `docs/hearthwild/RULES.md`, and the user-dispatched step before editing game code.
- The full specification is `docs/COZY_SANDBOX_PLAN.md`; execution order and explicit clarifications are in the packet pack.
- Implement only the dispatched step or requested repairs. Prerequisite steps require explicit user approval.
- Finish at READY_FOR_REVIEW with reproducible manual tests. Only the user may approve a step; passing automated tests is not approval.
- Never automatically start the next step, spawn another implementation agent, push, or deploy.
- Preserve unrelated edits and Hushlight. Vanilla ES modules, local Three.js, no engine/bundler/backend.
- Keep simulation independent of browser/rendering; all gameplay mutations use validated commands.
- Every step must be reachable and testable through the browser UI without console commands or gifted resources.
- Update `docs/hearthwild/STATUS.md` and the step's report with evidence and outstanding issues.
- Handoff documents are gitignored. Include them when moving work to another workspace or agent.
